  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. The fix is complete. \n\nThe issue was in the `extractMentions` function in `src/lib/mentions.ts`. It wasn't using the existing `withoutCode` helper function to filter out code blocks before extracting mentions. \n\nThe bug caused notifications to be sent whenever someone's name appeared as a word in a shell snippet inside a fenced code block, even though the docstring and tests explicitly stated that mentions inside code blocks should be ignored.\n\nBy adding `withoutCode(body)` before the regex matching, mentions inside both inline code (backticks) and fenced code blocks (triple backticks) are now properly ignored when extracting mentions for notifications. Since `resolveMentions` uses `extractMentions`, the notification fan-out also benefits from this fix automatically.",
